            <div xml:id="d410">

                <pb facs="0459" n="359" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg359"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.2311/145</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Peruvian Appointed Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Pezet</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation<anchor n="4" xml:id="d410-f1"
                    />]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-12-17"><hi rendition="#italic">December 17,
                        1919</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary</hi>: By direction of my Government I
                    have the honor to place in Your Excellency’s hands, the autograph letter<anchor
                        n="5" xml:id="d410-f2"/> of His Excellency the President of the Republic of
                    Peru, Senor Don Augusto B. Leguia, to His Excellency the President of the United
                    States of America informing him that he assumed the Executive Power October 12,
                    1919, on the strength of the election made by the people and upon taking the
                    oath required by law before the Legislative Chambers convened in National
                    Assembly.</p>
                <p>In delivering the said autograph letter to the august addressee, I beg you to add
                    my very sincere wishes to those formulated by His Excellency the President of
                    Peru that the relations between our countries be drawn as close as possible and
                    that the Government of this great Nation may extend its powerful aid to that
                    which has just been inaugurated in my country.</p>
                <p>I avail myself [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. A. Pezet</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
